Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||04-13-2001||11:55 AM||||I picked up my copy about 5 hours ago, and returned it 5 minutes ago. What a piece of... well, you catch my drift. My measily Cel@850, Voodoo3, 128Mb runs T2 at a whopping 10fps, after all patches and tweaks. T1 runs at 120fps on my system, so even though T2 is more complex, I don't accept a 95% framerate drop.<P>I've read the T2 newsgroups and the forums and basically, if you have a 3DFx card, you're screwed. If you have a Celeron, you're screwed. If you have anything less than a P3/1.5GHz + Geforce2 + 256Mb, you will not get framerates higher than 20fps outdoors.<P>This sucks. I'm <B>very</B> disappointed. I truly love Tribes 1, but I guess Tribes is now history for me.||||reg||13
Z||000004||COUNTIBLIS||04-13-2001||03:30 PM||||Cliff i had the same problem, it ran fine in solo but when i did a lan or multi, the frame rate sucked.  I have dsl, 600 athlon, 256 megs of ram, and i had to take it back.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count3.gif">  <P>1997 Mitsubishi Eclipse <BR>1997 Dodge Neon R/T<BR>1986 Pontiac Fiero Gt 3.1<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero Gt||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||04-13-2001||06:54 PM||||What really chops my high, is that on the box the minimum system requirements are listed as: P3/400, 64Mb, and OpenGl/D3D 3D Accelerator with minimal 8Mb. Well, that's fine if you want to run a frickin' slide show! My system is twice as powerful as that and it still ran like crap.<P>I'm not willing to upgrade my system for just one game. All other games I have (and that's quite a lot) run at a minimum of 100fps @ 800x600 with full detail on, even games like Unreal Tournament.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||COUNTIBLIS||04-13-2001||08:17 PM||||Yea, me either, Im now back in the market for a new multiplayer game online.  Any suggestions?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count3.gif">  <P>1997 Mitsubishi Eclipse <BR>1997 Dodge Neon R/T<BR>1986 Pontiac Fiero Gt 3.1<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero Gt||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||04-13-2001||08:32 PM||||I returned T2 and got Black & White instead. I had never heard of the game (I don't keep track of new games very much) but the salesperson said it was a great game. I played it for an hour or so and it's something competely different than the high-paced online games I usually play. I'm not sure yet if I like it (I haven't tried the multiplayer option yet) although it looks promising. There's some very funny stuff in it but I really miss the action.<P>For now I'm back to Tribes 1 although the number of players is decreasing rapidly. I heard today they are working on Unreal 2 (not to be confused with Unreal Tournament).<P>But there's one thing I have learned: I will never buy a game again that hasn't got a downloadable demo. I've spend too much money on games that I've played once and never again (returning games isn't so easy here in Holland).<BR>||||reg||1
